A script-level :PARAMETERS after a top-level statement fires
diag.parameters_first; a second script-level :PARAMETERS list fires it
again, since the first one counts as a statement.
-- input.ssl --
:DECLARE nAttempts;
nAttempts := 0;
:PARAMETERS sTarget;
:PARAMETERS nRetries;
:RETURN sTarget + LimsString(nRetries + nAttempts);
-- format --
:DECLARE nAttempts;
nAttempts := 0;
:PARAMETERS sTarget;
:PARAMETERS nRetries;
:RETURN sTarget + LimsString(nRetries + nAttempts);
-- diagnostics --
3:1-3:12 error parameters_first: Script-level ':PARAMETERS' must appear before top-level statements (leading ':PROCEDURE' blocks are allowed)
4:1-4:12 error parameters_first: Script-level ':PARAMETERS' must appear before top-level statements (leading ':PROCEDURE' blocks are allowed)
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
3:1-3:12 error parameters_first: Script-level ':PARAMETERS' must appear before top-level statements (leading ':PROCEDURE' blocks are allowed)
4:1-4:12 error parameters_first: Script-level ':PARAMETERS' must appear before top-level statements (leading ':PROCEDURE' blocks are allowed)
